<title>SRI LANKA: Three, six-month Sri Lanka T-bills ease at auction.</title>
<headline>Three, six-month Sri Lanka T-bills ease at auction.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The weighted average yield of three and six-month Sri Lankan treasury bills eased at Wednesday's auction, while 12-month yields were unchanged, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The auction was substantially oversubscribed, the bank added.</p>
<p>		   bids received   bids accepted  avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     3,079	     2,072	  18.17 (18.20)</p>
<p>    6 months	 304		  75	  18.02 (18.03)</p>
<p>    12 months    4,521	     2,886	  17.93 (17.93)</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets).</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
